 well as vapor recovery systems under EcoVapo brand. It also offers original equipment manufacturer equipment, including pumps, generator sets, air compressors, dryers, blowers, mixers, and valves; modular oil and gas wellsite facility solutions; and application systems, work processes, parts integration, optimization solutions, and after-sales support services. In addition, the company provides supply chain and materials management; inventory planning; integrated supply; integrated supply; product quality programs; manufacturer assessments; multiple daily deliveries; volume purchasing; truck stocking; technical support; training; just-in-time delivery; and on-site commissioning; after-market field repair and rental mobile pumping units; inventory and zone store management; order consolidation; product tagging and system interfaces tailored; supplier specifications; engineering of control packages; valve inspection and repair; product expediting, tracking and tracing; documentation services; and pressure testing services. It serves customers in the upstream, midstream, and Gas Utilities sectors, as well as downstream and industrial including crude oil refining, petrochemical and chemical processing, general industrials, pharmaceutical, mining, water/wastewater treatment, data centers, liquefied natural gas, and terminals and renewable natural gas facilities. The company was formerly known as NOW Inc. and changed its name to DNOW Inc. in January 2024. DNOW Inc. was founded in 1862 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David A. Cherechinsky CPA | CEO, President & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $570K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $27K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["DNOW Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.4B market cap on $2.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 17% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $134M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -23.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 87% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8713313161875946},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $7.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 67/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"DNOW (DNOW) Could Be 27% Undervalued After Its Q3 Earnings Beat","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-dnow/dnow/news/dnow-dnow-could-be-27-undervalued-after-its-q3-earnings-beat","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793985467.371,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"DNOW (DNOW) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/05/dnow-dnow-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793912294.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"DNOW Inc. Q3 2026 Revenue Surges to $1.337 Billion Amid Rising Costs","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/dnow-inc-q3-2026-revenue-surges-to-1337-billion-amid-rising-costs","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793902459.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"DNOW Stock Slides Into Focus After Mixed Earnings Report","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-dnow/dnow/news/dnow-stock-slides-into-focus-after-mixed-earnings-report","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793895937.27,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.628,"tier":0